# Security and privacy

Use this for auth, customer or staff data, uploads, invoices, webhooks, or logging.

- Authorize on the server for every query and mutation. A customer can access only their own resources. Staff are limited to their location membership. Unauthorized access returns 403 and leaks no record data.
- Launch roles are service advisor, technician, and manager/owner. Technicians work assigned repair orders. Refunds, staff management, settings, and the audit log are manager or owner actions.
- Do not store or log a card number or CVC. Take payment through the provider's hosted checkout or Payment Element. Verify webhook signatures and make handlers idempotent. Leave an invoice open until the provider confirms payment.
- Customer pages show only customer-safe notes and photos marked visible to the customer. Internal notes stay on the staff side.
- Rate-limit login, signup, booking, estimate requests, and password reset. Session cookies are `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, and `SameSite`.
- Write append-only audit events for estimate send and approval, repair-order status changes, invoice create, pay, and refund, role changes, and catalog or hours changes.
- Do not commit secrets. Keep personal data out of logs.
